!AH: this is only for C version. Not used in L version. 
!AH: changed to 0.96 in line with observation, but as said not relevent. 
!Meijer, W. J. M., van, E.W.J.M. Mathijssen, & van. (1995). Constraints to dry matter production in fibre hemp (Cannabis sativa L.). European Journal of Agronomy, 4(1), 109–117. https://doi.org/10.1016/s1161-0301(14)80022-1‌
 40.00 61.00  0.96  0.10                   PARMAX,PHTMAX,KCAN, KC_SLOPE 
! 40.00 61.00  0.68  0.10                   PARMAX,PHTMAX,KCAN, KC_SLOPE
!Note: Kcan can be overridden by value in Ecotype file, if present
!Kc_slope is the slope of Kcan with ratio of Rowsp:PlantSp (see DEMAND subroutine).
!Kc_slope is optional, default value is 0.10.
!AH: these are also only for C version.
  79.0  2.08 .0106                         CCMP,CCMAX,CCEFF; CO2 EFFECT ON PGCAN !AH: these are also only for C version.
!Alwin Hopf notes
!AH: the next two values are only for C photosynthesis. Not used in L photosynthesis
!AH: In general, better to use L photosynthesis (Y/XLMAXT etc.) according to KBJ
!left this leaf N effect on photo effect same as in Soybean. No data available for Hemp, need to look for more data 
!AH from KJB: The reduction of leaf photosynthesis is strictly related to the N concentration of leaf tissue, and depends on the N concentration relative to the two-point parabolic function.
