!*CARBON AND NITROGEN MINING PARAMETERS
!AH: from Ken Boote: NSTFAC was formerly locked in code to 0.70, now set to 0.60 for cotton.  
!This causes shift of partitioning to roots as a function of NSTRES.  
!You should also know that the NSTRES signal is now based on a 2-day running averaged rather 
!than a 1-day instantaneous value.  Reason is that NSTRES bounces and is a function of daily N supply and N demand.  
!N supply is rather constant function of RLD and soil N concentration, while N demand can 
!bounce up and down depending on variations in daily light driving photosynthesis.
!NMOBMX and NVSMOB are increased. first
 0.024  0.75  .260  .150  0.40  0.15   CMOBMX,CADSTF,CADPR1,NMOBMX,NVSMOB,NRCVR
    SD  0.60                           XPODF, NSTFAC
